    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bhjk3ac",
      "content": "Fundamentals of Nursing form the foundation of nursing practice. This area focuses on basic nursing principles, patient care techniques, infection control, vital signs monitoring, hygiene, bed making, patient safety, and basic clinical procedures. In RRB Nursing and other nursing competitive examinations, many questions are asked from vital signs, nursing process, infection control, patient positioning, hospital safety, and basic bedside procedures."
    },
    {
      "id": "dqexapc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Concept of Nursing"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vhtwjfq",
      "content": "Nursing is the art and science of caring for individuals, families, and communities to maintain or recover optimal health and quality of life."
    },
